  "claim": "The state where Jairos Jiri created facilities in the 1940s for disadvantaged and disabled people, in Southern Africa, whose capital is located in Salisbury, hosted the 1996 Currie Cup in which John David McPhun played.",
  "evidencia": "Page: John McPhun. Sentence: John David McPhun (born September 8, 1940 in Salisbury, Rhodesia) was a first-class cricketer who played for Rhodesia in the Currie Cup.\nPage: Rhodesia. Sentence: With its capital in Salisbury (now Harare), Rhodesia was considered a \"de facto\" successor state to the former British colony of Southern Rhodesia (which had achieved responsible government in 1923).\nPage: Jairos Jiri. Sentence: He started creating facilities in the 1940s for disadvantaged and disabled people in Rhodesia/Zimbabwe, using Christian principles of charity, patience and non-judgmental tolerance.",
